      "writtenOn": "2026-08-11T12:33:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The two cases are a bit different in my view.\n\nThe target branch may have been deleted while the change still exists, so `targetSha \u003d null` is valid. I think it would be wrong to raise an exception for this.\n\nThe meta ref is different because a change just cannot exist without it; that is an error, and returning `null` would hide an inconsistent state.\n\nWDYT?",
